## P18-V01 FastCodesHeader production source inventory — 2026-10-17T19:47:25Z

- Scanned the pinned Java client `remoting/src/main/java` source tree for
  production `FastCodesHeader` implementations. Exactly four were found:
  `PullMessageRequestHeader`, `PullMessageResponseHeader`,
  `SendMessageResponseHeader`, and `SendMessageRequestHeaderV2`.
- Each maps to an invoked Java fast/reflection fixture and a Rust comparison.
  The fixtures cover valid and missing fields plus representative conversion
  failures; Send V2 also covers inherited-field decode behavior and V1
  conversion.
- Rust implements mode-specific decoding for all four classes. The full
  current-revision P18-V02 suite verified these fixtures on code revision
  `fcc0f3f1`.
- This closes the bounded production `FastCodesHeader` inventory. Generic
  reflection decoding for other typed headers and broad bidirectional P18-V01
  source/API/settings/input/error/flow reconciliation remain open.

## Consumer offset header follow-up and full current-revision P18-V02 — 2026-10-17T20:26:39Z

- Repository: /Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/trio/rocketmq-classic.
- Branch: phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate.
- Starting code HEAD: 51168d2b. Final code HEAD for this record: 3beabab0.
- Java oracle: /Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/3rd/rocketmq, RocketMQ 5.5.1 source commit efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9, read-only.
- Scope: P18-V01 consumer offset typed-header decode behavior and current-revision P18-V02 gates.

## Oracle finding and code commits

- Source inspection confirmed QueryConsumerOffsetRequestHeader, UpdateConsumerOffsetRequestHeader, and QueryConsumerOffsetResponseHeader do not implement FastCodesHeader. RemotingCommand therefore uses the generic reflective path regardless of its useFastEncode hint. The decoder catches missing or invalid per-field conversions; Boolean.parseBoolean maps malformed setZeroIfNotFound to false; these three checkFields implementations are no-ops. Java's String, Integer, and Long header values can therefore remain null after direct decoding despite CFNotNull annotations.
- Added OffsetHeaderDecodeModeFixtures and fixtures/remoting/offset-header-decode-modes.json. Rust models the direct-decoded fields as nullable, follows per-field reflection recovery under either mode hint, and checks response offset at the consumer RPC result boundary.
- Fixture SHA-256: 2e911e6369ef5260ac73ad7ecbd3db9b38d190f8b080b5d36fc46997e7f20ddb.
- Code commit: b59431e4 fix(protocol): match Java offset header decoding.
- The first full Linux workspace run exposed a timeout in consumer_lookup_uses_timeout_mutated_after_runtime_construction because its first NameServer route lookup also used the mutated 150 ms timeout. The test now warms and verifies the route under the original 3000 ms timeout before applying the Java fixture's 150 ms value to the Broker RPC. The focused test and all 17 runtime_lookup tests pass.
- Test-only commit: 3beabab0 test(core): isolate live lookup timeout case.

